# SPC website — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit real values.
# Server-side only unless explicitly marked NEXT_PUBLIC_ (client-safe by
# design). Never add the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix to anything else.

# --- HubSpot (direct REST API) ---
HUBSPOT_PRIVATE_APP_TOKEN=
# Portal 244173183. Scopes needed: crm.objects.contacts read/write (+ tasks).

# --- Assessment submit (via Make.com webhook) ---
MAKE_ASSESSMENT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Make scenario that receives the assessment on submit and creates the HubSpot
# ticket. Body: full assessment (photo base64 stripped) + top-level pdf_url +
# ticket_body.

# --- Supabase (assessment storage) ---
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# On submit the PRIVATE "assessment-pdfs" bucket receives, all keyed by reportId:
#   <customer>-<date>-<reportId>.pdf    the rendered report (signed URL -> pdf_url)
#   <customer>-<date>-<reportId>.json   the full raw assessment, so it can be
#                                       reopened and re-rendered later
#   photos/<reportId>/NN-<label>.jpg    each captured photo, as its own file
#   index/<reportId>.json               pointer the /r/<reportId> viewer reads
# Service role key is server-only. Smoke-test after setting these:
# GET /api/health/supabase

# --- Public report viewer (/r/<reportId>) ---
# REPORT_BASE_URL=
# Absolute base for the viewer link that goes into the HubSpot ticket and gets
# forwarded to customers. Optional: falls back to the Vercel production alias.
# SET THIS AT DOMAIN CUTOVER (https://sunsetpoolcare.com) — see next.config.ts.
# HEALTHCHECK_TOKEN=
# DELIBERATELY LEFT UNSET — please don't "fix" this without reading why.
# If set, /api/health/* requires ?token= (or an x-healthcheck-token header).
#
# /api/health/supabase is the most useful diagnostic in this build: it has
# identified two production outages (Aug 24, Sep 9) by pasting a URL into a
# browser — no tooling, no deploy, no log access. Gating it behind a token that
# has to be looked up first is exactly the friction you don't want at the moment
# something is broken. On an unindexed vercel.app subdomain that trade-off is
# worth it; the endpoint only writes and deletes a throwaway object.
#
# TODO AT DOMAIN CUTOVER: set this, alongside REPORT_BASE_URL above. A real
# public domain changes the calculus — the endpoint does perform real storage
# writes, so an open one there is a spam surface.

# --- Supabase keep-alive cron ---
CRON_SECRET=
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. Vercel sends this as `Authorization: Bearer <value>`
# when it triggers the daily cron at /api/cron/supabase-keepalive. That route
# FAILS CLOSED — with this unset it refuses every request, so it can never become
# an open endpoint a stranger can use to drive storage operations.
#
# The cron exists because a free-tier Supabase project auto-pauses after ~a week
# of inactivity, which has already caused two outages (Aug 24, Sep 9). A paused
# project still reports configured:true and fails every storage call with a 544
# DatabaseTimeout — so "configured" never means "healthy". Schedule lives in
# vercel.json; daily is the most frequent the Hobby plan permits.
# Generate one with:  node -e "console.log(crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"

# --- Google Drive (service account) ---
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
GDRIVE_ASSESSMENT_FOLDER_ID=
# Service account JSON (stringified) + target folder for assessment PDFs.

# --- Claude API — NO LONGER REQUIRED ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# The AI presentation layer (notes polish + summary paragraph) has been removed.
# The report renders the tech's own words verbatim, so nothing in this codebase
# reads this variable any more. Safe to delete from the hosting environment.

# --- Post-service review page (/review) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_REVIEW_URL=https://search.google.com/local/writereview?placeid=REPLACE_WITH_PLACE_ID
# Where the 4-5 star thank-you page sends happy customers ("Leave a Google
# Review", opens in a new tab). Client-safe: it's the public review link.
# If unset, the button is simply hidden.

# --- Analytics (client-safe, added in content phase) ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=

# --- Office report review (/assessment/review/<reportId>) ---
REVIEW_ACCESS_CODE=
# Shared code the office types once to reach the review-and-regenerate screen.
# Enforced server-side: the page won't load a report and the save endpoint won't
# accept anything without it. LEAVING THIS UNSET DISABLES THE SCREEN ENTIRELY —
# it fails closed rather than admitting everyone. See docs/fixing-a-report.md.
